    <grid>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "name": "1 column layout",
  "sections": [
    {
      "grid": "12",
      "rows": [
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "309e2d4b-2d7d-4f87-ba89-b73f65ff57bf",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<div class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"758bl\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\">\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\">\n<div class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"><hr />\n<p>Roadlab E Serviços Limitada, Roadlab's operation in Mozambique, will be performing earthworks investigations for a critical tailings storage facility at Balama graphite mine from 2021 to 2023.</p>\n<p>Balama graphite mine is the source of 75% of the world's graphite supply.</p>\n<p> </p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        },
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "87b51188-70a7-41cc-b36e-1ac1258ba7d4",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<p><span class=\"heading-h3\">Project Information</span></p>\n<p>Located in Northern Mozambique Cabo Delgado Province, 260km west of Pemba, Balama graphite mine is simple open pit mine that produces 94 – 98% fixed carbon graphite concentrate. It the largest graphite mine in the world.</p>\n<p>Graphite is a good conductor of heat and electricity and is useful in electronic products such as batteries and solar panels. It used primarily in pencils and lubricants such as grease.</p>\n<p>Balama is owned by TWIGG Exploration and Mining Limitada, a subsidiary of Syrah Resources based in Australia.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 1899,
                    "udi": "umb://media/353c3906a24340ff8073ed9f79251956",
                    "image": "/media/aa2dynkd/inside-facilities19201080.png",
                    "caption": "Inside the facilities. Image available at syrahresources.com.au/balama-project"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": "media"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                }
              ],
              "styles": null,
              "config": null
            }
          ],
          "styles": null,
          "config": null
        },
        {
          "name": "Article Full",
          "id": "51c1cd0c-48b2-41a9-be33-9b4eecbe8a08",
          "areas": [
            {
              "grid": "12",
              "controls": [
                {
                  "value": "<hr />\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "<p><span class=\"heading-h3\">Roadlab's Contribution</span></p>\n<p>Roadlab E Serviços Limitada will help ensure a high level of quality control on the earthworks of the new tailings storage facility at Balama graphite mine.</p>\n<p>Our on-site facility will provide compaction and material testing services for more than 1.5million cubic meters of engineered fill. These efforts will provide technical insights critical to ensuring the projects success and it's alignment with international best practice as recommended by the ICMM.</p>\n<p>Roadlab will also be providing a high level of proof in risk mitigation for the earthworks component of the installation.</p>\n<p> </p>",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 1906,
                    "udi": "umb://media/4d6f49facfbc4d72816c3ca1894f7475",
                    "image": "/media/5reh4tn2/tailings19201080.jpg",
                    "caption": "The tailing storage facility site. Image available at syrahresources.com.au/balama-project"
                  },
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "media",
                    "view": "media"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": "",
                  "editor": {
                    "alias": "rte",
                    "view": "rte"
                  },
                  "styles": null,
                  "config": null
                },
                {
                  "value": {
                    "focalPoint": {
                      "left": 0.5,
                      "top": 0.5
                    },
                    "id": 1908,
                    "udi": "umb://media/bb3c1584b6ba4b2f8dd9e2fd30e5f2b3",
                    "image": "/media/qikdzo30/roadlab-team-edited-jpeg.png",
                    "caption": "Roadlab E Serviços Limitada staff at Balama graphite mine."
                  },
                  "editor": {
